meta {
  name: delete me (whole account)
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

delete {
  url: {{bff_url}}/api/me
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Full account deletion, orchestrated in self-healing order:
  collection purge, then auth wipe (identities + refresh families),
  then the user row, then session teardown (jti denylisted, cookie
  cleared). Expect 204 and a dead session: "me" answers 401 until the
  next "dev login". A mid-sequence failure answers 502 with the
  session intact so the request can simply be retried.

  Fixture accounts are disposable by design: the next dev login as
  alice recreates a fresh, empty account. Do not point this at an
  account whose collection you care about.
}
